{"id":2620848,"docketId":24886,"caseName":"Turner v. Enrille","caseNameFull":"","slug":"turner-v-enrille","docketNumber":"","dateFiled":"1799-08-09","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1799,"scdbId":"1799-007","direction":"Conservative","votesMajority":6,"votesMinority":0,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":null,"natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":23,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":2620848,"type":"majority","typeCode":"010combined","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":789,"isHtml":true,"text":"<div>\n<center><b><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"6606945\"><a href=\"/opinion/6725727/turner-v-president-of-the-bank-of-north-america/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Turner v. President of the Bank of North America\">4 U.S. 7</a></span> (____)</b></center>\n<center><b><span class=\"citation no-link\">4 Dall. 7</span></b></center>\n<center><h1>Turner, Administrator,<br>\nversus<br>\nEnrille.</h1></center>\n<center><p><b>Supreme Court of United States.</b></p></center>\n<center></center>\n<p><span class=\"star-pagination\">*8</span> For the defendant in error, Dallas lamented the obvious irregularities on the face of the record.</p>\n<p>By the COURT.</p>\n<p>The decision in the case of Bingham v. Cabot et al. must govern the present case. Let the judgment be reversed with costs.</p>\n</div>"}],"citations":[]}